\begin{lemma}[Evolve the supplied approximation]\label{lem:annular-evolving}
\uses{lem:annular-static,prop:ramps-global,thm:ramps-uniform-jets}
\lean{PoincareMT.m64EvolvingApproximation_from_M63}
For a supplied polygonal family approximation, its actual flattened
curves generate the shrinking ramp family. The number of sides,
initial curves, and initial area-error annuli remain those of that
same approximation.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Apply the ramp existence and family estimates to the selected smooth
flattenings. No new approximation is chosen, so the initial-area
estimate is the one from Lemma~\ref{lem:annular-static}.
\end{proof}

